WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.957
Morning, Ziad.

00:00:00.957 --> 00:00:02.394
Sunday the fifteenth.

00:00:02.394 --> 00:00:08.959
A cold, bright one, with a lazy morning and an afternoon where the calendar double-books itself.

00:00:08.959 --> 00:00:11.490
Here's one to chew on while you move.

00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:18.398
When the bot commits the finished audio every morning, why doesn't that push kick off another render?

00:00:18.398 --> 00:00:19.765
Answer's at the end.

00:00:19.765 --> 00:00:23.595
Weather's dry all day, topping out in the upper forties.

00:00:23.595 --> 00:00:25.032
The wind's the thing.

00:00:25.032 --> 00:00:34.607
Northwest around fifteen, with gusts near thirty from midday into the early afternoon and again around seven, so any ride west will be work.

00:00:34.607 --> 00:00:35.564
Okay, the day.

00:00:35.564 --> 00:00:38.095
Nothing on the calendar this morning.

00:00:38.095 --> 00:00:42.814
At one, the Play Fair at Bogart House is on there, running till five.

00:00:42.814 --> 00:00:46.302
And a housewarming is on there from three to eight.

00:00:46.302 --> 00:00:53.825
The two overlap, so a couple of hours at the fair and then heading over would cover both, if you're up for it.

00:00:53.825 --> 00:00:54.782
Alright, news.

00:00:54.782 --> 00:00:55.808
Just two today.

00:00:55.808 --> 00:00:57.176
The big one in tech.

00:00:57.176 --> 00:00:59.228
Jensen Huang is out at Nvidia.

00:00:59.228 --> 00:01:02.442
The company said Thursday he resigned as C.E.O.

00:01:02.442 --> 00:01:08.119
and left the board, effective immediately, after more than thirty years running it.

00:01:08.119 --> 00:01:09.213
No reason given.

00:01:09.213 --> 00:01:15.505
The finance chief is filling in as interim C.E.O., and the board named its first ever chair.

00:01:15.505 --> 00:01:16.805
The timing is wild.

00:01:16.805 --> 00:01:19.198
Nvidia reports earnings on Tuesday.

00:01:19.198 --> 00:01:21.387
Nvidia makes the chips most A.I.

00:01:21.387 --> 00:01:23.644
runs on, so this one ripples far.

00:01:23.644 --> 00:01:25.354
And one that's just cool.

00:01:25.354 --> 00:01:34.381
SpaceX caught Starship's upper stage with the giant arms on its launch tower in Texas, after a flight of more than twenty-two hours.

00:01:34.381 --> 00:01:40.537
It's the first time the top half has come back from orbit and been grabbed out of the air.

00:01:40.537 --> 00:01:45.598
That's the piece that has to be reusable for the whole thing to get cheap.

00:01:45.598 --> 00:01:48.675
Okay, here's the main thing for next weekend.

00:01:48.675 --> 00:01:54.284
Chama Mama, the Georgian restaurant, has a big new Bushwick spot on Morgan Avenue.

00:01:54.284 --> 00:01:55.925
It's three rooms in one.

00:01:55.925 --> 00:02:03.790
A dining room built around a traditional Georgian oven, a bar and lounge, and a bakery up front called Let's Chama.

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:05.773
The bakery's the easy way in.

00:02:05.773 --> 00:02:09.125
Georgian pastries, savory and sweet, plus coffee.

00:02:09.125 --> 00:02:11.724
So a cold Saturday morning works fine.

00:02:11.724 --> 00:02:22.256
If you go for dinner, the move is khachapuri, the boat of bread filled with melted cheese, a runny egg yolk, and a pat of butter you stir in at the table.

00:02:22.256 --> 00:02:30.121
And they lean into Georgian wine, especially amber wine, which is white wine made like red, with the skins left in.

00:02:30.121 --> 00:02:32.857
It comes out orange and a little earthy.

00:02:32.857 --> 00:02:35.182
Today's challenge is a making one.

00:02:35.182 --> 00:02:37.986
Build a tiny light modifier out of trash.

00:02:37.986 --> 00:02:40.312
A cereal box, some foil, and tape.

00:02:40.312 --> 00:02:44.894
Make a little bounce card, white on one side and foil on the other.

00:02:44.894 --> 00:02:49.339
Then put a mug or a glass by a window and try both sides as fill.

00:02:49.339 --> 00:02:51.665
White goes soft, foil goes punchy.

00:02:51.665 --> 00:02:58.230
Five minutes, no buying anything, and you'll have a pocket reflector for the next tabletop shot.

00:02:58.230 --> 00:03:01.992
Okay, something new today, and it's right in your lane.

00:03:01.992 --> 00:03:08.421
Focus stacking, the trick behind those product shots where everything is sharp, front to back.

00:03:08.421 --> 00:03:09.720
Here's the problem.

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:15.397
Get close to something small, like a fork, and your depth of field gets razor thin.

00:03:15.397 --> 00:03:18.543
The tines are sharp and the handle melts away.

00:03:18.543 --> 00:03:21.347
Stopping way down helps, but only so far.

00:03:21.347 --> 00:03:26.476
Past about f eleven or so, most lenses start to soften everything a little.

00:03:26.476 --> 00:03:31.537
That's diffraction, light bending as it squeezes through the tiny opening.

00:03:31.537 --> 00:03:34.341
So instead of one shot, you take a bunch.

00:03:34.341 --> 00:03:37.214
Camera locked on a tripod, nothing moving.

00:03:37.214 --> 00:03:44.942
You start with focus on the nearest edge, then nudge focus back a little each frame, until you reach the far end.

00:03:44.942 --> 00:03:47.883
Each frame has one thin slice that's sharp.

00:03:47.883 --> 00:03:56.432
Then software lines them all up and, for every spot in the picture, keeps the pixels from whichever frame was sharpest there.

00:03:56.432 --> 00:04:01.767
It figures that out by looking for the most fine contrast, the crispest edges.

00:04:01.767 --> 00:04:08.059
Out comes one image that's sharp everywhere, at the aperture where your lens is at its best.

00:04:08.059 --> 00:04:08.880
Two catches.

00:04:08.880 --> 00:04:14.693
First, focusing changes the framing slightly, so things grow a bit as you move focus.

00:04:14.693 --> 00:04:17.976
The software has to rescale each frame to match.

00:04:17.976 --> 00:04:19.891
Second, shiny stuff is hard.

00:04:19.891 --> 00:04:28.577
On silver, reflections move as focus shifts, so you can get halos or ghosty patches where a highlight lands in different spots.

00:04:28.577 --> 00:04:32.338
That's why a lot of people retouch those areas by hand.

00:04:32.338 --> 00:04:37.057
So: calendar says the Play Fair at one and the housewarming at three.

00:04:37.057 --> 00:04:38.562
Make that bounce card.

00:04:38.562 --> 00:04:46.290
The answer: the commit lands in a folder the trigger ignores, and the bot's own key can't start a new run anyway.

00:04:46.290 --> 00:04:48.000
Have a good Sunday, Ziad.
